  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the file set establishing the dependency graph for this refactor:\n\n**Confirmed edges:**\n- **babel \u2192 next.js**: `packages/next/package.json` pins `@babel/core@7.18.0`, `@babel/traverse@7.18.0`, `@babel/generator@7.18.0`, `@babel/types@7.18.0`, `@babel/parser@7.12.11` as *devDependencies* (also pinned in root `package.json` `resolutions`). These get vendored via `packages/next/taskfile-ncc.js` (ncc bundling) into `next/dist/compiled/babel/*`, which `packages/next/src/build/babel/loader/transform.ts` imports directly (`traverse`, `generator`, `core-lib-normalize-file`, etc.) and runs through `packages/next/src/build/babel/loader/index.ts` as the webpack babel-loader. This is a real but **pinned/vendored** edge, not a live semver range \u2014 a parser AST change only reaches Next.js after Next.js bumps its devDependency pins and re-runs the ncc vendoring step.\n- **webpack \u2192 next.js**: `packages/next/package.json` devDependency `webpack@5.86.0` (matching root resolutions) is vendored the same way into `next/dist/compiled/webpack/webpack`, imported directly in `packages/next/src/build/webpack-config.ts`.\n- **babel \u2192 webpack: NOT an edge for this change.** `webpack`'s `package.json` `dependencies` use `acorn`/`acorn-import-assertions` for its core JS parser \u2014 no `@babel/*` package appears there. `@babel/core` and `@babel/preset-react` are *devDependencies only*, used for webpack's own test fixtures/examples, not its shipped module-parsing pipeline. A new Babel parser AST node does not reach webpack's runtime.\n\nInternal babel propagation order (from each package's `dependencies`): `babel-parser` (emits the node) \u2192 `babel-types` (node/visitor-key definitions) \u2192 `babel-generator`/`babel-traverse` (both depend on types; traverse also depends on parser+generator) \u2192 `babel-core` (depends on all three) \u2192 `plugin-syntax-decorators`/`plugin-proposal-decorators` (consume core).",
